    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "## Key Considerations\n\n**Pressure Band:** The difference between maximum and minimum tank pressure is critical. A larger pressure band allows:\n- Better buffering of consumption variations\n- More air storage capacity\n- Reduced compressor cycling\n\n**Typical Pressure Bands:** 10 psig is common; 15-20 psig provides better buffer capacity.\n\n**Unit Conversions:**\n- 1 ft³ = 0.02832 m³\n- 1 gallon (U.S.) = 3.785 liters\n- 1 psig = 0.069 bar"
    }
  ]
}